Z||000000||Sage||02-05-2001||05:45 PM||||Some time ago,(I believe around 12/99), I posted asking if anyone ever heard of a "factory" rasberry paint.<P>A friend of mine bought a gt that had this paint on it, and said that the man he bought it from claimed that it was original.  I doubted it when he told me, that is why I asked the forum.  It is not my car, I never made the claim that it was original paint.  I only said that it was a very good paint job.  The reason I am "updating" this post is because I had an occasion to find out first hand, as I put a clutch in the car for him several months ago.  I just wanted to let you all know that you were right, and basically, so was I when I doubted it.  It is a repaint.  I felt bad for him, that he was lied to, and fell for it, but none the less, it is without a doubt a repaint.  The paint code reflected this also, but I still had my doubts until the clutch job, when I removed the rear facia, to insert a bar to lift the car with.  There was definatly med red metalic overspray.  It is still one of the best after factory paint jobs I've ever seen, but IS "after" factory!  Just thought someone would like to know they were right!<P>         Have a good one!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||02-05-2001||06:04 PM||||I knew it all along. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Thanx for being square with us about it.  Sorry for your friend?  I wouldn't be.  Unless he was specifically looking for factory original paint, he probably got a bargain.||||reg||1
